RACING
Lewis Hamilton Ferrari Error: How He Reached the Podium
Published
11 minutes ago
on
October 5, 2026
By
Marcelo Lagos
Lewis Hamilton turned a major Ferrari strategy mistake into a third-place finish at Sepang after starting the race on slick tires in wet conditions.
Ferrari’s risky call nearly ruined Hamilton’s race
Lewis Hamilton went from believing his race was effectively over to celebrating another Formula 1 podium.
The Ferrari driver finished
third at Sepang
, despite falling deep into the field after Ferrari chose slick tires for the start on a wet track. Hamilton had qualified on the front row and started
second
, but the decision immediately backfired.
The race was held at Sepang as the
Bahrain Grand Prix in Malaysia
, creating one of the most unusual events of the 2026 calendar. Heavy rain delayed the start and left teams facing difficult tire decisions.
Lewis Hamilton drove the Ferrari SF-26 at Sepang during the chaotic 2026 race weekend.
Hamilton later admitted that the decision was painful.
He had looked at the track after the delayed start and could still see water on the asphalt. Even so, he believed the surface would dry quickly enough to make slicks the correct choice.
Ferrari also expected
Max Verstappen to make the same call
.
That assumption proved costly.
Hamilton dropped down the order on slick tires
The conditions were still too wet when the race finally got underway.
Drivers on intermediate tires immediately gained a major advantage. Hamilton’s Ferrari struggled for grip, and he dropped around
15 positions
, falling as far as 18th in the early stages.
At one point, Hamilton was roughly
a minute behind the leaders
.
That appeared to end his chances of a strong result.
Hamilton had to control the Ferrari on a slippery track after the initial slick-tire gamble failed.
Ferrari eventually offered Hamilton the opportunity to pit.
The seven-time World Champion chose to
stay out
.
That decision became one of the most important moments of his race. Instead of making another stop while the conditions were still changing, Hamilton kept the soft tires running and waited for the track to improve.
The gamble required patience.
As the asphalt dried, the Ferrari’s pace improved. Hamilton began recovering positions while saving the advantage of having completed fewer pit stops.
Safety Cars changed the race
The race then became even more unpredictable.
A Safety Car closed the gaps and gave Hamilton another opportunity to recover. Ferrari changed his tires at that point, and Hamilton continued moving forward as the field compressed again.
He eventually found himself fighting
Isack Hadjar for fourth place
.
A later Safety Car created another opening.
Hamilton returned to soft tires and used their pace to attack Hadjar. He eventually passed the Red Bull and moved into the podium positions.
The comeback was extraordinary considering where he had been earlier.
Hamilton recovered from the back of the field to finish third for Ferrari at Sepang.
Charles Leclerc also recovered strongly.
The other Ferrari initially switched to intermediates after the slick-tire mistake. Contact and a damaged front wing made his race even more difficult, but Leclerc eventually finished
fourth
, giving Ferrari both cars inside the top four.
That was a major recovery for the Italian team.
Ferrari went from a disastrous opening phase to a double top-four finish.
Hamilton gives Ferrari credit after the mistake
For Hamilton, the key difference came after the initial strategy error.
He believes Ferrari
did not repeat the mistake
later in the race.
The pit stops were cleaner. The timing improved. The team also reacted well to the Safety Car periods.
Hamilton praised the mechanics and the engineers for recovering from the difficult opening phase.
That recovery transformed the weekend.
Ferrari had looked capable of fighting at the front after Hamilton qualified second. Instead, the early tire decision appeared to destroy those hopes before the race had properly settled.
Yet the team remained calm.
From one minute behind to another podium
The numbers tell the story.
Hamilton started
second
. He then dropped to the back of the field and was around a minute behind the leaders. By the finish, he was standing on the
third step of the podium
.
Max Verstappen won the race, with Kimi Antonelli second and Hamilton third. Ferrari’s Leclerc followed in fourth.
The result also gave Hamilton his
208th career podium
, extending his record at the top of Formula 1’s all-time podium list, according to the race reports.
More importantly, it showed how quickly a race can change when weather, tire strategy and Safety Cars interact.
Hamilton’s result did not erase Ferrari’s opening mistake. It did, however, demonstrate that the team was able to recover from it.
The
Lewis Hamilton Ferrari comeback at Sepang
turned a strategy error into another podium, with the seven-time World Champion recovering from roughly a minute behind the leaders to finish third after one of the most chaotic races of the 2026 season.
