electric vehicle industry
faces slowing growth, higher financing costs, infrastructure challenges, and increased competition. While GM continues to invest in EV technology, the company — like several other automakers — has adjusted timelines and production volumes to reflect changing market conditions.
The Fairfax plant transition underscores how legacy automakers are balancing long-term electrification goals with the continued profitability of
gas-powered vehicles
