Michigan · 83 counties, local assessors, equalization departments, treasurers and deed offices
Find the Assessor, Tax Bill, Deed or Parcel Map
Michigan does not use one county-auditor portal for every property. Assessment records normally begin with the city or township assessor, county Equalization may provide countywide maps and sales data, local treasurers collect current taxes, and county treasurers handle delinquent accounts.
This guide shows how to identify the correct local unit, search by parcel number, address or owner, understand Michigan values, check the current 2026 deadlines, locate recorded deeds and choose the correct review or appeal process.
