Michigan terminology correction:
Searching for a “Michigan county auditor” may lead to the wrong department. Use the city or township assessor for the assessment record, county Equalization for countywide assessment support, and the appropriate treasurer or Register of Deeds for the next task.
Quick answer: identify both the county and local unit
Find the property’s county, city or township first. Open the official county website, locate Equalization, GIS or Property Search, and then confirm which local assessor maintains the parcel. Search with the parcel number when available, verify the local unit and address, and save the complete property record before paying taxes or researching deeds.
1
Find the county
Use the land’s physical location, not the owner’s mailing address.
2
