Delinquency, forfeiture and foreclosure
Prior-year unpaid taxes require a county payoff
The last statewide calendar date for local treasurers to collect 2025 taxes was March 2, 2026. Taxes returned delinquent then moved into the county collection process, where additional fees and monthly interest can apply.
After local collection
Contact the county treasurer for the complete amount rather than paying the amount printed on an old bill.
Forfeiture
Real property is generally forfeited during the second year of delinquency, adding costs and additional procedures.
Foreclosure
Taxes still unpaid by March 31 of the third year can result in foreclosure by the responsible governmental unit.
